          <td colspan="2" height="30" background="newsheader.jpg"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b><font size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tales from the Halls of Testing</font></b></font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr bgcolor="#330033"> 
          <td width="60%"><font size="2"><i><font face="Verdana">by <A href="javascript:createWindow('memberdetails.asp?id=1','profile','scrollbars,width=550,height=500')"><font color=yellow>Falqour Thornwalker</font></a></font></i></font></td>
          <td width="40%"> 
            <div align="right"><font size="2"><b>Posted: 12/12/2001 2:52:11 AM</b></font></div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td colspan="2">
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><B><p align="center"><font size="2" face="Verdana"><img src="../newscaps/softovbattle3sm.jpg" align="left"><img src="../newscaps/softovbattle2sm.jpg" align="right"><b>Screenshots of SoF's very first raid in the Halls of Testing!</b></font></p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2">Thanks again, CIW, for guiding us through our very first ToV romp!</font></p>                                                                                                                                                                                         </B></font><P>
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><BR><BR><p><font size="4" face="Times New Roman"><img src="../newscaps/softovbattle2.jpg" width="300" height="225" align="right">Last Sunday, the Spirit of Fire Expeditionary Regulars traversed the dangerous Wastes of the West, past the Sirens Grotto, to venture to the holy place of worship for all of Wurmkind, the Temple of Veeshan. Few mortals dare to tread upon this sacred ground, but the Dragons of the Claws of Veeshan permitted us to enter.</font></p><p><font size="4" face="Times New Roman">Once inside this temple of the goddess of the sky, we were confronted by legions of fearsome winged creatures, the likes of which most of our party hadn't yet beheld. To our relief, they appeared friendly, and beckoned us to enter. Our guides, a platoon of masterfully trained men and women from the Clan Icewind battlehoard, led us to the grand door that separated us from our fate. Beyond the door, echoes of screaming dragons, magical explosions and the clanging of metal battlements could easily be heard from the outer hall. The stench of death hung low in this place, and though we were afraid, we had faith in our elite guides.</font></p><p><font size="4" face="Times New Roman"><img src="../newscaps/softovbattle3.jpg" width="300" height="225" align="left">Upon entry into the Halls of Testing, we encountered a detachment from the Crusaders of Plilo, who were there to destroy the vile and wicked Dozekar the Cursed, a malevolent being of pure evil. Leaving the Crusaders to their task, we ventured on, deeper into the winding and twisting maze. Along the way, many particularly unfriendly beasts confronted our troops, only to be felled by our army's wrath. </font></p><p><font size="4" face="Times New Roman">This venture into the unknown proved to be well worth the effort. We obtained several pieces of ordinary armor that our allies in Skyshrine offered to enhance into truly formidable pieces of equipment.</font></p><p align="left"><font size="4" face="Times New Roman">We learned much from our guides during this adventure, lessons we won't soon forget. The Spirit of Fire would like to formally thank Grandmaster Matthi O'oem for overseeing and arranging the entire mission, and for giving us a taste of what is in store for us in the future. We'd also like to thank the rest of the elite squad from the Clan for contributing their time and effort during this raid, namely, Grayshadow, Krystof, Aild, Taludana, Castore and Gwel.</font></p><p align="center"><img src="../newscaps/matthitov.jpg" width="400" height="339"><br><font size="2" face="Verdana"><b><font size="4"><i>Grandmaster Matthi O'oem</i></font></b><br><i><font size="1">(easily, the most impressive creature we saw that night!)</font></i></font></p><p align="center"> </p><p align="center"><font size="4" face="Times New Roman"><img src="../newscaps/SoFTov.jpg" width="450" height="174"><br><b><font size="2" face="Verdana">The Spirit of Fire Expeditionary Regulars</font></b></font></p>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       </font>
</td>
